.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt SAFE-FILL-HOST 1
.Os POSIX.1-2017
.Sh NAME
.Nm safe-fill-host
.Nd native messaging host that copies a safe password to the clipboard
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is started by Firefox on behalf of the tatl extension, through the
native-messaging manifest
.Pa ~/.mozilla/native-messaging-hosts/safe_fill.json .
It is not meant to be run by hand.
.Pp
It reads one native-messaging frame from stdin (a 32-bit length in
native byte order, then that many bytes of JSON), builds the store path
.Pa passwords/<origin>/<username> ,
asks
.Xr safe-agent 1
to decrypt that one path with the
.Sq D
command, and hands the plaintext to
.Xr wl-copy 1
with
.Fl -paste-once .
It writes one frame back and exits.
.Nm
never holds the key and never opens the store; the agent does both.
.Pp
A request can instead ask for the usernames saved for an origin, which
the agent lists with the
.Sq L
command; see
.Sx REQUEST .
Nothing is decrypted for these.
.Pp
After a successful copy a child process runs
.Ql wl-copy --clear
after
.Dv WL_CLEAR_DELAY_SEC
seconds (10 by default) as a backstop.
.Sh REQUEST
The request is a JSON object of string members.
The optional
.Ar op
member selects what is asked; without it the request is a fill:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li {"origin":"example.org","username":"alice"}
.It Li {"op":"fill","origin":"example.org","username":"alice"}
Copy the password of
.Pa passwords/example.org/alice .
.It Li {"op":"user","origin":"example.org"}
If exactly one entry is saved for the origin, copy its username, with
.Fl -paste-once
as for a password.
No
.Ql wl-copy --clear
is scheduled: a username is not secret, and the delayed clear would
wipe a password copied right after it.
.It Li {"op":"list","origin":"example.org"}
Reply with the usernames saved for the origin.
Nothing is copied.
.El
.Pp
The parser is deliberately small:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Each member is found as the first occurrence of
.Ql \(dq<name>\(dq:\(dq
with no whitespace around the colon; the sender must emit compact JSON.
.It
Values may not contain a backslash, so no escapes, and may not be empty.
.It
.Ar origin
is at most 253 bytes of
.Ql "A-Z a-z 0-9 . : - _" ,
does not start with
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql \&: ,
and contains no
.Ql .. .
A port is part of the origin
.Pq Ql example.org:8443 ;
default ports are not.
.It
.Ar username
is at most 255 bytes, contains no
.Ql / ,
.Ql \e ,
control characters or
.Ql .. ,
and does not start with
.Ql \&. .
.El
.Pp
These are the same rules
.Xr safe-fill-migrate 1
applies when it names entries, so every migrated entry can be filled.
.Sh REPLY
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Li {"success":true}
The password is on the clipboard.
.It Li {"success":true,"username":"alice"}
.Pq Ar user
The username is on the clipboard.
.It Li {"success":true,"usernames":["alice","bob"]}
.Pq Ar list
The usernames saved for the origin, possibly none.
.It Li {"success":false,"error":"<code>"}
Nothing was copied.
.It Li {"success":false,"error":"<code>","usernames":[...]}
.Pq Ar user
Nothing was copied, because
.Ar code
is
.Li no_entry
(the list is empty) or
.Li ambiguous
(it has several names; the extension lets the user pick one).
.El
.Pp
Names are JSON strings in which only
.Ql \(dq
is escaped, since a valid username contains no backslash and no control
character.
.Pp
Error codes:
.Bl -tag -width "clipboard_failed" -compact
.It Li bad_frame
The frame was empty, short, or longer than 64 KiB.
.It Li bad_request
A member is missing, empty, or contains a backslash.
.It Li bad_op
.Ar op
is not
.Li fill ,
.Li user
or
.Li list .
.It Li bad_origin , bad_username
A value failed the checks above.
.It Li path_too_long
The resulting store path does not fit.
.It Li no_agent
No agent socket was found, or it failed validation.
.It Li prctl_failed , landlock_failed , seccomp_failed
The sandbox could not be set up.
.It Li oom , mlock_failed
The secret buffer could not be allocated or locked.
.It Li agent_failed
The agent refused, was locked, or the entry does not exist or does not
authenticate.
For
.Ar user
and
.Ar list :
the agent refused or was locked; a missing origin is an empty list.
.It Li no_entry , ambiguous
.Pq Ar user
See above.
.It Li empty_secret
The entry decrypted to nothing.
.It Li clipboard_failed
.Xr wl-copy 1
could not be run or failed.
.El
.Sh AGENT SOCKET
In the hardened build
.Pq Ic make install-hardened
the socket path is compiled in
.Pq Dv AGENT_SOCK_PATH ,
by default
.Pa /run/safe/browser/agent.sock ,
and the environment is not consulted for it.
Otherwise
.Nm
uses
.Ev SAFE_SOCK ,
then the path written by the agent in
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/safe/sock .
.Pp
The socket must not be owned by root, its directory must not be owned
by root and must not grant write to group or any access to others.
Outside the hardened build both must also be owned by the effective
uid.
After connecting,
.Nm
checks with
.Dv SO_PEERCRED
that the agent runs as the socket's owner.
.Sh CLIPBOARD BACKEND
The backend is chosen when
.Nm
is built, never at run time:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It wl-clipboard-rs (default)
Runs
.Ql wl-copy --paste-once --sensitive .
Needs a compositor with a data-control protocol (wlroots-based
compositors, KDE).
.It wl-clipboard, the C implementation
Built with
.Ql WL_CPPFLAGS=-DWL_BACKEND_C .
Required on GNOME/mutter, which has no data-control protocol; this is
the usual case on Ubuntu.
Runs
.Ql wl-copy --paste-once -t text/plain ;
there is no
.Fl -sensitive .
This
.Xr wl-copy 1
buffers its input in
.Pa /tmp/wl-copy-buffer-XXXXXX/stdin ,
so the sandbox grants
.Pa /tmp
for this build only, and the password is written to that file for as
long as it is on the clipboard.
If
.Pa /tmp
is not a tmpfs, that file is on disk.
.El
.Pp
A host built for one backend and run with the other fails without an
obvious error.
.Ic safe-wl-backend check
compares the installed
.Xr wl-copy 1
with the installed host;
.Ic safe-wl-backend flags
prints the
.Ev WL_CPPFLAGS
value for the installed
.Xr wl-copy 1 .
.Sh HARDENED PROFILE
The hardened host is installed as
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/safe-fill-host ,
mode 6750, owner
.Em _tatl ,
group
.Em safe-tatl .
Only members of
.Em safe-tatl
can run it.
The set-group-id bit lets it reach the browser agent's socket, and the
agent admits
.Em _tatl
for
.Sq D
only
.Pq Fl u ,
restricted to
.Pa passwords/
.Pq Fl p .
Before running
.Xr wl-copy 1 ,
the child drops to the real uid and gid and checks that the
.Em _tatl
ids can not be regained.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SAFE_UNSAFE_MLOCK"
.It Ev SAFE_SOCK
Agent socket (not in the hardened build).
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location of the agent's
.Pa safe/sock
pointer file (not in the hardened build).
.Xr wl-copy 1
is always given
.Pa /run/user/<real uid> ,
not this value.
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Passed to
.Xr wl-copy 1
if it contains no
.Ql / .
No other variable reaches
.Xr wl-copy 1 .
.It Ev SAFE_UNSAFE_MLOCK
If set, a failure to
.Xr mlock 2
the secret buffer is not fatal.
Ignored when the host runs set-user-ID or set-group-ID.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the password or username was copied or the list was sent, 1
otherwise.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The origin comes from the extension.
Nothing checks it against the page the user is looking at, so a
compromised extension can ask for any
.Pa passwords/*
entry, one request at a time, and nothing limits the rate.
Any process that can run
.Nm
can do the same.
The same goes for the usernames saved for an origin it names: listing
is not limited to the page in front of the user either, though it
cannot enumerate the origins themselves.
.Pp
A clipboard reader in the same session that wins the race against the
paste sees the password.
The backstop
.Ql wl-copy --clear
clears the clipboard whatever it holds by then, including something
the user copied in the meantime.
.Pp
On Linux the host runs under Landlock and seccomp; see
.Pa README
for what they allow.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr safe 1 ,
.Xr safe-agent 1 ,
.Xr safe-fill-migrate 1 ,
.Xr wl-copy 1
.Sh AUTHORS
Part of this fork of Willy Goiffon's
.Xr safe 1 ;
see
.Pa README .
